<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.8.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00992</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.8.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6d0b9cdc-1959-4b1e-8ff0-c96a56258c13</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para>Use the following information to answer questions 1 - 5.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>The temperature was recorded at several times during the day. Function \(T\) gives the temperature in degrees Fahrenheit, \(n\) hours since midnight. A graph for this function is provided.</quote>
     </para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_11_13_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_36fb9833-9b22-48d3-ba94-bfb28c0d0c2e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For the interval from \(n = 1\) to \(n = 5\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Negative</para>
            <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Negative</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_17ce8bbf-5675-409a-988f-8f28ec382260" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For the interval from \(n = 5\) to \(n = 7\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Positive</para>
            <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Positive</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d64e57ef-2350-47f5-a377-889332659ba1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For the interval from \(n = 10\) to \(n = 20\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Positive</para>
            <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Positive</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_95188503-775f-411f-891e-da2d26468ed6" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For the interval from \(n = 15\) to \(n = 18\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Zero</para>
            <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Zero</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_9f6200ba-6973-4e97-b2d9-676e4d513843" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For the interval from \(n = 20\) to \(n = 24\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Negative</para>
            <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Negative</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <para>The graph below shows the total distance, in feet, walked by a person as a function of time, in seconds. Use this information to answer questions 6 - 7.</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Distance Graph">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_11_13_02.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_5cfaa9e4-f352-4656-b90d-04385efdf1c0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Given the graph of total distance walked as a function of time, was the person walking faster between 20 and 40 seconds or between 80 and 100 seconds?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Between 80 and 100 seconds</para>
            <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Between 80 and 100 seconds</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a8564426-ea5c-4301-b4ef-b89e94193f78" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Was the person walking faster between 0 and 40 seconds or between 40 and 100 seconds, based on the given graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Between 0 and 40 seconds</para>
            <para>Try Again. Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Between 0 and 40 seconds</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_9b6b5602-f18c-4172-b78e-dabe92a3384e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 8 - 11, use the following scenario.</para>
            <para>
              <quote>The height, in feet, of a squirrel running up and down a tree is a function of time, in seconds.</quote>
           </para>
            <para>Match each description with a statement about the average rate of change of the function for that interval.</para>
            <para>The squirrel runs up the tree very fast. The average rate of change is -</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The average rate of change is large and positive.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: The average rate of change is large and positive.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_53a323b9-b7d1-4a6a-a5b0-cb5ad212906a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The squirrel starts and ends at the same height. The average rate of change is -</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The average rate of change is zero.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: The average rate of change is zero.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="ab53564e-2bb2-4af8-bf28-151d03a9cfb4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The squirrel runs down the tree. The average rate of change is _____.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!The average rate of change is negative.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: The average rate of change is negative.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_441417cc-6a8a-401e-b12f-52bfcbc23d0d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The squirrel runs up the tree slowly. The average rate of change is _____.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.1 - 4.8.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: The average rate of change is small and positive.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d47c6530-0e2a-4c55-97e4-ce0e632f01f7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The function \(P\) gives the percent of voters ages 18 to 29 years old who participated in the election in year \(t\).</para>
            <para>The percentage of voters ages 18 to 29 who participated in each United States presidential election between the years 1988 and 2016 is shown in the table.</para>
            <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
              <tgroup cols="9"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
              Year
           </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
              1988
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              1992
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              1996
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              2000
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              2004
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              2008
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              2012
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              2016
            </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
              Percentage of voters ages 18–29
           </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
              35.7
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              42.7
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              33.1
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              34.5
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              45.0
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              48.4
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              40.9
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              43.4
            </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
            <para>Determine the average rate of change for \(P\) between 1992 and 2000.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>1.025 percent per year</para>
            <para>-1.025 percent per year</para>
            <para>0.35 percent per year</para>
            <para>-2.4 percent per year</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!  -1.025 percent per year</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities  4.8.1 - 4.8.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is -1.025 percent per year.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6c3fd095-c018-4f05-a8fb-49b8fc6bce96" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Some points from a linear function, \(f(x)\), are listed in the table below. What is the rate of change of this linear function?</para>
            <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
              <tgroup cols="5"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
              \(x\)
           </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
              0
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              5
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              10
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              15
            </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
              \(f(x)\)
           </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
              4
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              6
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              8
            </entry>
                  <entry>
              10
            </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>2</para>
            <para>\(\frac25\)</para>
            <para>\(-\frac25\)</para>
            <para>6</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\frac25\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(\frac25\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b792dc6a-15c9-4fce-a1c4-2b5ea3eff48a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <newline/>
            <para>Find the rate of change of the function, \(g(x)\), graphed below.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is -3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6fd19ceb-d534-44db-818a-3beafba2fdd0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the rate of change of the function \(h(x)= 4x -7\)?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
